title:: BMSnapShot
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - represents an automation snapshot
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMSnapShot represents a snapshot in an automation sequence. Its public methods are all defined in its superclass.

Under normal circumstances you will not need to make these directly, but will rather create them through a link::Classes/Automation/BMSnapShotSeq::.

See also: link::Classes/Automation/BMAbstractSnapShot::, link::Classes/Automation/BMArbitraryStartSnapShot::, link::Classes/Automation/BMSnapShotSeq::, link::Classes/Automation/BMAbstractAutomator::, link::Classes/Root Classes/BMControl::, link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractController::, link::Classes/Automation/BMSnapShotSliders::, link::Overview/Time References and Automation::